// ============================================================================
// LORELINE PRESS TURN + COMMANDER ENGINE
// Generic, data-driven combat prototype
// ============================================================================
//
// LAYERING — the one rule of this project:
//
//   engine/  pure rules, no content. Never names a character, a skill or an
//            encounter; every number it uses comes from data/.
//   data/    all the content and all the tuning. Editing it changes the game;
//            editing engine/ changes the game's laws.
//   scenes/  the Loreline presentation shell — beats, choices, text. It only
//            calls engine functions and interpolates their results.
//
// Import order is free: Loreline resolves functions at call time, and every
// import shares one global namespace (which is also why two beats may never
// share a name across files).
//

import engine/state
import engine/press_turn
import engine/actors
import engine/skills
import engine/rewards
import engine/score
import engine/combat
import engine/ai
import engine/ui

import data/rules
import data/skills
import data/actors
import data/encounters
import data/registry

import scenes/combat_flow
import scenes/score_screen


// Boot: load the content databases, then let the player pick a demo.
//
// The three `commander_demo` entries are the same encounter with three
// different openings — that is the whole point of the menu: initiative decides
// which side spends the first round's icons, and against an even squad that
// single difference is felt for the entire fight.

beat Start
  initializeDatabases()

  PRESS TURN + COMMANDER ENGINE

  Rules demonstrated here:
  - Press Turn action economy
  - Weak / Crit / Miss / Null / Repel / Drain / Pass
  - AGI order and neutral initiative
  - Smirk
  - every enemy group can designate one Commander
  - killing the Commander ends the battle immediately
  - surviving enemies give no XP / reward
  - Commander final HP can go negative on the killing blow
  "- Overkill % = negative HP / Commander max HP, capped at 100%"

  choice
    Commander demo — Player Advantage
      startEncounter("commander_demo", "player")
      -> CombatRouter

    Commander demo — Neutral Initiative
      startEncounter("commander_demo", "neutral")
      -> CombatRouter

    Commander demo — Enemy Advantage
      startEncounter("commander_demo", "enemy")
      -> CombatRouter

    // Same rules, one enemy with bonus icons instead of three bodies — the
    // solo-boss shape of the same action economy.

    Boss extra-Press demo
      startEncounter("boss_press_test", "player")
      -> CombatRouter

    End
      -> .
